The use case

Do not say “sample app.” Give it a business story.

Suggested use case

Order Processing Platform

Services:

api-service: receives order requests
worker-service: consumes SQS jobs and processes orders
notification-service: fake email/webhook notifier
postgres: stores order metadata and status
redis: caching / idempotency keys / rate limiting
s3: stores generated invoice/report files

Flow:

Client hits API through ALB ingress
API validates request
API writes order row to PostgreSQL
API publishes job to SQS
Worker consumes job
Worker processes order and updates DB
Worker writes artifact to S3
Notification service sends simulated notification
Metrics/logs/traces collected
Failures go to DLQ or error table

That gives you sync + async + stateful + observable architecture. That is what matters.

